                <TextValueRun styleId="681583:17" text="IDEA: a parchment courtroom. A small grey figure in a scarlet-stained garment stands before a tall bench; papers of evidence stack up beside them on `evidence`. On `righteous` the judge's gavel falls and a gold word stamps across the bench. On `wait` the frame tilts and pushes in on the figure's face, puzzled. On `job` the question writes itself above the bench, the only text: How should man be just with God?" name="brief" id="681583:20"/>
            </Text>
